Found while fixing #67, pre-existing and unrelated to it.

Cmd/Context.pm:121 builds its "recently completed" section by grepping for
terminal statuses inside @active_tasks -- but @active_tasks is defined as the
NON-terminal tasks. The intersection is empty by construction, so the section
has never had a single entry in any board.

Not a regression from the terminal-status work: it was equally empty when the
terminal statuses were hardcoded. It just becomes visible once you go looking at
how terminal status is used.

Fix is to grep the full task list instead, and decide what "recently" means --
kanban-md bounds it by completion timestamp. Note the completed stamp itself is
unreliable on a board with custom statuses; see the empty-strings ticket.
Geschlossen durch cd4d043/58f0fc7: recently-completed scannt jetzt das ganze Board, tagesgranular geboundet durch --days. Haengt am completed-stamp-Fix (#67-Leftover) aus demselben Commit. t/108.
